	(text "RJ45 CABLE MAPPER  rev A  rixnobis"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "9ef92b2e-79c0-4b89-972c-59cec30d4e93")
	)
	(text "Touch a flying wire to PAD1; the LED for its 8P8C pin lights. ULN2803A sinks each\nLED. PAD at 5V through 1k, so a wire grounded at the far end draws 5 mA, not a short.\nA finger bridging pad and wire (~1 Mohm) leaves the ULN input far below its ~2.7 V on\nthreshold, so only metal-to-metal contact lights an LED. Two shorted wires light two."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "5a2fe8bd-2dcd-4cd6-a466-17ff2391fde8")
	)
	(text "RJ45 jack (RCH RC01937, LCSC C708652) is the only through-hole part, hand-soldered.\nEverything else is SMD, JLC-assembled. The jack is shielded, so its shell is a 9th\nchannel (Q1, LED S): a shielded cable's drain wire lights S."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 134.62 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c28f40b1-458c-4d84-bbcc-f008b8a82c0f")
	)
